* Op-amp macromodels for schem2spice. Behavioral, NOT vendor models: see models/map.yaml.

* NJM2068 (New JRC dual low-noise op-amp), one section.
* Datasheet typicals: GBW 27 MHz, open-loop gain 110 dB, input bias current 200 nA
* (bipolar NPN input), output swing about +/-13.5 V on +/-15 V, supply current
* 5 mA per package (2.5 mA per section). Offset voltage (0.3 mV typ) is not modelled.
* Single-pole: gm stage into R1||C1, gain = gm*R1 = 3.16e5 (110 dB),
* pole set so that GBW = gm / (2 pi C1) = 27 MHz. Output: behavioral source limited to
* 1.5 V inside the rails, Rout 50 ohm. The gain node is bounded by clamps to fixed
* +/-25 V references, NOT to the supply pins: rail-referenced clamp diodes form a
* path between V+ and V- and gave a false "collapsed rails" operating point when the
* supply is fed through a resistor (P601). Output current is drawn from ground, not
* the rails (supply current = IQ only). Pins: non-inverting, inverting, V+, V-, output.
.subckt NJM2068 inp inn vcc vee out
IBP inp 0 200n
IBN inn 0 200n
RIN inp inn 1Meg
G1 0 n1 inp inn 1m
R1 n1 0 316Meg
C1 n1 0 5.9p
VCH ch 0 25
VCL cl 0 -25
DH n1 ch DCLAMP
DL cl n1 DCLAMP
B1 n2 0 V = max(min(V(n1), V(vcc) - 1.5), V(vee) + 1.5)
ROUT n2 out 50
IQ vcc vee 2.5m
.model DCLAMP D(IS=1f N=1)
.ends NJM2068
